IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc6-s150-definitions.l4 -- s 150, the definitions of Part V (Sexual Offences, Public Morals and Disorderly Conduct).
-- "In this Part" scopes them (R3 of PLAN.md), so they are encoded here and not in the keel's section 2.
-- All four say "includes", so each answers JUST TRUE for a case it names and NOTHING for any other case: a list that is not closed.
-- (`s 150 guardian` and the others: JUST FALSE would claim that a person outside the list is NOT a guardian, which the text does not say.)

§ `s 150 In this Part`

-- src:2995 | guardian includes any person who has in law or in fact the custody or control of another person; (tuteur)
@ref Criminal Code s 150 "guardian" (src:2995)
GIVEN `the person has in law the custody or control of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has in fact the custody or control of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150 guardian` MEANS
    IF `the person has in law the custody or control of another person` OR `the person has in fact the custody or control of another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "guardian includes"

-- src:2996 | public place includes any place to which the public have access as of right or by invitation, express or implied; (endroit public)
@ref Criminal Code s 150 "public place" (src:2996)
GIVEN `the public have access to the place as of right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public have access to the place by an express invitation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public have access to the place by an implied invitation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150 public place` MEANS
    IF    `the public have access to the place as of right`
       OR `the public have access to the place by an express invitation`
       OR `the public have access to the place by an implied invitation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "public place includes"

-- src:2997 | sexual organs includes genital organs, breasts that are or appear to be female breasts and the anal region; (organes sexuels)
@ref Criminal Code s 150 "sexual organs" (src:2997)
DECLARE `s 150 part of the body` IS ONE OF
    `s 150 genital organs`
    `s 150 breasts that are female breasts`
    `s 150 breasts that appear to be female breasts`
    `s 150 the anal region`
    `s 150 a part of the body that is none of those`

GIVEN `the part of the body` IS A `s 150 part of the body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150 sexual organs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the part of the body`
    WHEN `s 150 genital organs` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 150 breasts that are female breasts` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 150 breasts that appear to be female breasts` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 150 the anal region` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 150 a part of the body that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "sexual organs includes"

-- The charge for admission is not an element ("whether or not any charge is made for admission"), so the function does not take it.
-- src:2998 | theatre includes any place that is open to the public where entertainments are given, whether or not any charge is made for admission. (théâtre)
@ref Criminal Code s 150 "theatre" (src:2998)
GIVEN `the place is open to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `entertainments are given at the place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150 theatre` MEANS
    IF `the place is open to the public` AND `entertainments are given at the place`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "theatre includes"
